>Somewhere along the journey into the depth of the dungeon, my barbarian
>"sensed" someone was pleading for help. Now he was at level 19, and had
>no clue as to what to do. I heard there was a mine and a quest to
>complete but had not encountered any. Was this normal? Should I go down
>further or was I missing something important?
>
When you 'sensed' a plea for help, you should've been told to
look for a '...ic portal', which would probably be on the same
level where you got the request.  Better see if you can find it again.
If you no longer remember which level that was, your problem is
now much harder.  Visit all the squares of the board that you can.

As far as the mine, the answer is not to go down, but to go Up.
Just don't accidentally leave the dungeon.  You should find some
alternative place to wander into.

In summary, this game really has its ups and downs.

